    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1476">

                <pb facs="0959" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/95.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Edwards to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad Juarez</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 19, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 19. This Consul visited General Villa in his private office
                    this afternoon and informed him of instructions of Honorable Secretary of State
                    Bryan, at the request of British Ambassador. General Villa stated that he was
                    anxious that my Government and the British Government should know the facts with
                    reference to William Benton and that he is dead. That Benton came to his house
                    armed and attempted to kill him. Villa produced large pistol which he said
                    Benton brought with him. I will convey the facts to the family and send full
                    particulars to the Department by next mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
